# Graph-only OneDrive (hard constraint)

**OneDrive Desktop is not available** on race-day laptops, Adam’s Windows VM, or any environment this app targets. Do not treat it as a fallback, diagnostic source, or layout oracle.

## Product rule

- Cloud I/O = **Microsoft Graph** only (`/me/drive`, MSAL sign-in inside this app).
- Local race cache = **`C:\S2F\Library`** + Active under **`C:\S2F\RaceDay`** — filled by Graph checkout / index, never by mirroring a Desktop sync folder.
- User-facing “OneDrive” means **cloud files via this app**, not the Windows OneDrive client.

## Agents must not

- Probe, read, rsync, robocopy, or “verify against” `C:\Users\…\OneDrive` (or `OneDrive - …`) for app data, vendor secrets, race packs, or folder layout.
- Assume Files On-Demand hydrate, Desktop settle waits, or Explorer sync status matter for Finish / checkout / mid-race.
- Diagnose “file missing on laptop” by looking under the Desktop tree — use Graph GET/list or `C:\S2F\…`.
- Reintroduce `OneDriveSyncMonitor`, hydration helpers, or Finish “wait for Desktop sync” copy — those were removed.

## When changing sync / checkout / Admin

Ask: “Does this path assume a local OneDrive Desktop folder exists?” If yes, delete that path or rewrite it to Graph + `C:\S2F`.

